SUMMARY:The Liar’s Bench Songwriter’s Series
DESCRIPTION:An intimate monthly listening experience at The Olde Bartley House.\n\nInspired by the stories, music, and community spirit behind Brown County’s legendary Liar’s Bench, these events bring together songwriters and listeners for afternoons of tall-tales, original music, coffee and community.\n\nPull up a chair. Listen awhile.\n\nDates: Every last Friday of the monthTime: 4-6pm (staying open an hour later for these events)\n\nMay 29, 2026Father Kentucky\nA poet, folk-singer, bluegrass wannabe picker, FATHER KENTUCKY sings for all those who’ve been up and down and all places in between.\nFor him, a song isn’t just something you sing. They’re something to get lost in, to be found in, to revel and cry and make you fall in love with friends and strangers all the while.\n
URL:https://browncounty.com/events/the-liars-bench-songwriters-series/
CATEGORIES:Entertainment,Happening,Live Music
LOCATION:96 S Van Buren St, Nashville, IN 47448
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncounty.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/OBH-Dietrich--scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
