SUMMARY:Painting Selma’s Garden
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the T.C. Steele State Historic Site for a day of art, inspiration, and celebration!\n🗓 Date & Time: Saturday\nJune 13th, 2026\n10:00 AM – 5:00 PM – Artists at work, paintings available for purchase all day\n5:00 PM – Centennial Celebration Reception featuring the play “Selma and the Painter” in the Steele Studio*\n📍 Location:\nT.C. Steele State Historic Site\n🎟 Reception Tickets*:\n$40 per person – reservations required.\nEvent Highlights:\nFrom 10am until 5pm, watch Indiana’s top artists bring Selma’s garden to life on canvas, for free!\nAt 5pm, enjoy a celebratory reception with live performances of the play, refreshments, and a chance to purchase artwork from the day’s paint-out.\nExplore the historic House of the Singing Winds and gardens.\nThis is a perfect day to celebrate art, history, and community. Don’t miss it!\nReception is $40 per person and can be purchased at https://9529a.blackbaudhosting.com/9529a/Painting-Selmas-Garden-13Jun2026\n
