SUMMARY:Brown County 4-H Fair
DESCRIPTION:The Brown County 4‑H Fair is an annual community tradition celebrating youth achievement, agriculture, and local pride. This family‑friendly event brings together exhibitors, families, and visitors for a week filled with education, entertainment, and classic fair fun.\n\nGuests can enjoy 4‑H project exhibits, livestock shows, and hands‑on learning experiences that showcase the hard work and dedication of Brown County youth. The fair also features food, activities, demonstrations, and special events that highlight the county’s agricultural heritage while offering something for all ages.\nWhether you’re supporting local 4‑H members, exploring exhibits, or simply enjoying time with friends and neighbors, the Brown County 4‑H Fair is a celebration of community, tradition, and the next generation.\nCarnival Hours: Mon-Fri 6-10pm ; Sat5-9pm\n4-H Exhibit Building & Commercial Areas: Mon-Sat 6-10pm\nParking $2 per vehicle, $10 per vehicle Weekly Pass\n\n
URL:https://browncounty.com/events/brown-county-4-h-fair/
