SUMMARY:Brown County Art Gallery Children’s Art Camp
DESCRIPTION:Give your young artist the chance to explore their creativity this summer at the Brown County Art Gallery Summer Art Camp! Open to students in 2nd–12th grades, this two-week camp offers hands-on learning in a variety of artistic disciplines.\nCamp Dates:\n\n\nGrades 2–5: June 15–26\n\n\nGrades 6–12: July 6–17\n\n\nSession Times:\n\n\nMorning Session: 9:00 AM – 1:00 PM\n\n\nAfternoon Session: 1:00 PM – 4:00 PM\n\n\nFull-Day Option: 9:00 AM – 4:00 PM\n\n\nTuition:\n\n\nHalf-Day Camp: $160 per two-week session\n\n\nFull-Day Camp: $200 per two-week session\n\n\nSibling Discount: $20 off each additional child\n\n\nCamp Activities Include:\n\n\nPainting, drawing, printmaking, mixed media\n\n\nClay & 3D art, portrait study, and portfolio development\n\n\nArt history and STEAM-integrated projects\n\n\nInteractive field trips and gallery tours\n\n\nLocation: Brown County Art Gallery, One Artist Drive, Nashville, INRegister Today: Call 812-988-4609 or email brncagal@gmail.com\nSpace is limited—register early to secure your spot!\nProudly supported by:Brown County Community Foundation, Indiana Arts Commission, and Indiana Heritage Arts\n
